                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TL:DR I enjoyed playing this game 10/10. Fun and interactive, have a marioparty levels of feeling to it. Great nostalgia while still being fresh in concept.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWARNING!!! ****** GRADE A LEVELS OF SHITPOSTING IS REFERED IN THIS REVIEW***** \n                                I made this as a joke and for shits and giggles only\n\nWhen noticing this hidden gem after searching purchasing my 4th copy of Champions of Breakfast i stumbled across on this little gem and decided that the pocket change price tag I decided to purchase the title. I walsed through the U.I and found it charmly simple. The art was cute and quirky. It reminded me of my fourth wife back in the day. \n\nBut suddenly it all faded to black. I woke up tied to a chair, I yelled \"Hello!\" nobody answered me. I yelled again and there it was 2 men in black ski-masks. It was my Teacher in highschool I had in a class we called in swedish \"Dator och nätverksteknik\" and I recognized his voice, Robin? I asked just to see a response and you could see the regret in his eyes. I look around me and realized that there must have been other students here who bought the game. People I called classmates and even friends, Alexander, Andreas, Hugo, William and even Henry. Yes even the dredded Ernests who I once called an ally on the battlefield. \nI was there tied to a chair with handcuffs barely reaching the very keyboard I am writing this review at held gunpoint by the teacher I onced called \"chill\" he used to be cool but after knowing the things he was capable of I could no longer take it. I broke free decided to run, betray my comerads and friends to be able to continue this review. I thought I would be safe here in my cabinet in the woods but Quicksave is after me, demanding a good review so here goes my last breath as an honest and my credability as a proffesional reviewer.\n\n\nSo after a long time playing of the release of this game, I really enjoyed the greatness of this game and I must say this game is pure perfection and crisp artwork, the flawless A.I and fun and intuitive gamedesign, the marioparty feeling i got from it gave me such joy. This is what I would say if Robin gave me an A in all the classes so do we have a deal mr Robin? This great review for my freedom and an A in your classes. \n\nSincerly a very scared Jonas from TE 15.",
